/**
 * Generated by orval 🍺
 * Do not edit manually.
 * Leaflow Assistant API
 * Conversations with agents that operate the Leaflow platform, plus their folders, tasks, files and
 * chat-app channels.
 *
 * A conversation is a thread. A person talks to the main thread; the agent in it can start subagents,
 * which are threads too and run on their own: stopping the main thread does not stop them, and each
 * subagent tells its parent when it ends. A thread runs in turns; each turn records the model and
 * reasoning effort it used and its token usage.
 *
 * Models come from the Canopy catalogue. A new thread uses the model it names, the caller's default
 * from /api/v1/settings, or the first catalogue model that can run an agent. Reasoning models take one
 * of three efforts — low, medium or high — which are sent to the model unchanged.
 *
 * Read a thread's state with get-thread and its transcript with list-thread-items. Follow both live
 * over the WebSocket described under /api/v1/realtime/tickets. list-thread-messages outlines the
 * person's messages for navigating a long conversation.
 *
 * Upload large files with /api/v1/uploads: read /api/v1/upload-configuration first, send exact-sized
 * parts, then complete the upload and send its attachment id in a message.
 * OpenAPI spec version: 2.0.0
 */
